1 OCCU ex mistress of King Frederick III of Denmark.  Created Baroness of Løvendahl in 1683 by King Christian V
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT https://lex.dk/Margrethe_Pape  - Baronesse af Løvendal.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margrethe Pape''', Friherreinde af Løvendal var datter af Nicolaus von Pape, hoffmester for det adelige frøkenkloster i Itzehoe (3 røde hjerter i gull) og hans hustru Anna.
2 CONT
2 CONT Før sit ægteskab med dronning Sofie Amalie havde Frederik III en frille, den holstenske Margrethe Pape, senere gift med amtsforvalteren Daniel Hausmann i Segeberg. Hun blev i 1683 af Christian V udnævnt til friherreinde af Løvenda
2 CONC hl.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Margrethe Pape (1620–1684) was a Danish baroness. She was the mistress of King Frederick III of Denmark and the mother of Ulrik Frederik Gyldenløve.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margrethe Pape became the lover of Frederick prior to his marriage and succession to the throne. She married the official, amtsforvalter of Segeberg and etatsråd Daniel Hausmann (d. 1670). In 1683, Christian V of Denmark granted h
2 CONC er the title Baroness of Løvendal.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://da.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margrethe_Pape
2 CONT
2 CONT Margrethe Pape, fødsels- og dødsår ukendt, Frederik 3.s elskerinde. Deres forhold blev indledt, før Frederik blev gift med Sophie Amalie og senere konge, og sammen fik de i 1639 sønnen Ulrik Frederik Gyldenløve. I 1683 udnævnte Ch
2 CONC ristian 5. Margrethe Pape til baronesse af Løvendal. Senest i 1652 blev hun gift med amtsforvalter i Segeberg, etatsråd Daniel Hausmann (d. 1670).
2 CONT
2 CONT (google Translated) Margrethe Pape, year of birth and death unknown, Frederik 3's mistress. Their relationship was initiated before Frederik married Sophie Amalie and later king, and in 1639 they got their son Ulrik Frederik Gylde
2 CONC nløve . In 1683 Christian 5. appointed Margrethe Pape to the baroness of Løvendal. By 1652, she was married to the county administrator in Segeberg, councilor Daniel Hausmann (d. 1670).
2 CONT
2 CONT http://denstoredanske.dk/Danmarks_geografi_og_historie/Danmarks_historie/Danmark_1536-1849/Margrethe_Pape
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederik III, 18.3.1609-9.2.1670, King of Denmark and Norway from 1648; son of Christian 4. and Anna Cathrine , married to Sophie Amalie of Braunschweig-Lüneburg in 1643.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of the successor and Christian 4. in respectively. June 1647 and February 1648, the stands and councils discussed the terms of Frederick's election for a long time, and on July 6, 1648 he was hailed as king and sig
2 CONC ned his final handhold , while the crowning took place on November 23.
2 CONT
2 CONT Leon Jespersen: Frederik III in The Great Danish , Gyldendal. Downloaded June 22, 2019 from http://denstoredanske.dk/index.php?sideId=79617
2 CONT ===Familie 1===
2 CONT
2 CONT * Frederik III Konge af Danmark og Norge - f. 18 mar. 1609, Haderslevhus Slot - d. 9 feb. 1670, Københavns Slot
2 CONT
2 CONT Gift: ikke-ægteskab 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Børn===
2 CONT
2 CONT # Ulrik Frederik Gyldenløve - f. 20 jul. 1638, Bremen, Germany - d. 17 apr. 1704, Hamburg, Germany 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Familie 2===
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daniel Hausmann - d. 1670, Itzehoe, Schleswig-Holstein, Germany 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Gift'': ca. 1649 - Segeberg, Schleswig-Holstein, Germany  
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Børn===
2 CONT
2 CONT #  Friedrich Hausmann - f. ca. 1649,   d. 25 apr. 1689
2 CONT # Gesilla Hausmann - f. ca. 1649, Germany  - d. 13 nov. 1672, Segeberg, Schleswig-Holstein, Germany
2 CONT # Caspar Herman Hausmann - f. 10 jan. 1653, Schleswig, Schleswig-Holstein, Germany - d. 9 sep. 1718, Oslo - Kristiania, Norge
2 CONT
