3 CTRY Scotland
1 BURI
2 DATE AFT 20 NOV 1406
1 DEAT
2 DATE 20 NOV 1406
2 ADDR
3 CITY Forbes
3 CTRY Scotland
1 OCCU Justiciary in Aberdeen, of the Black Lip. Castle Forbes by River Don, Aberdeen, Viscount, Ridder, Sheriff og retsmediciner
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sir Alexander de Forbes was Justiciary of Aberdeen, and Coroner of that county married a daughter of Kennedy of Dunure.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Sir Knight John “Black Lip” de FORBES Lord Of Forbes
2 CONT
2 CONT http://venitap.com/Genealogy/WebCards/ps31/ps31_181.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John de Forbes, knight . 
2 CONT
2 CONT * - He is mentioned as Lord of Forbes, 20 August 1387,  
2 CONT * - as knight in a letter from King Robert III, 6 April 1391, in which a perambulation of the boundaries of certain lands belonging to the Bishop of Aberdeen on the one part, and the lands of Forbes on the other is ordered.  
2 CONT * - In 1394 he was appointed justiciary and Coroner of Aberdeenshire.  
2 CONT * - On 2 January 1404-5 he made a certain payment to Alexander Stewart, Earl of Mar, as directed by a court held by the duke of Albany. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His name frequently appears as a witness to charters up to May 1406, but before 20 November of that year he was succeeded by his eldest son.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is said to have married Elizabeth or Margaret Kennedy of Dunure, 
2 CONT
2 CONT by whom he had four sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. Sir Alexander
2 CONT * 2. Sir William Forbes, ancestor of Lord Pitsligo
2 CONT * 3. Sir John Forbes, who obtained the thanedom of Formartin and land of Tolquhoun by marriage with Mariota, daughter and heir of Sir Henry Preston of Formartin, knight, widow of Alexander Chisholm, and was ancestor of the Forbes 
2 CONC of Tolquhoun, Foveran, Watertoun, Colloden, and others.
2 CONT * 4. Alaster, styled ‘Alaster Cam,’ who married, about 1409, Katharine, the daughter and heiress of Sir Henry Cameron of Brux, by whom he obtained that estate and was ancestor of the Forbes of Brux, now represented by the families
2 CONC  of Skellater and Inverernan. On 24 December 1409 he had a charter of the lands of Glencarve and others. He died about 1466,
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Forbes is also said to have had three natural sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. Duncan, ancestor of the family of Auchintoul.
2 CONT * 2. Malcolm, ancestory of Culquhary and others.
2 CONT * 3. John, a man of violence, who, it is said, was killed by his brother Sir Alexander by command of the King .
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: THE SCOTS PEERAGE, ed. by Sir James Balfour Paul, Vol IV, Edinburgh, 1906, pp. 46-47. < [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04paul/page/46/mode/2up Archive.Org] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Nævnes 1372. Fik fra jarlen Thomas af Mar en del landområder i Aberdeenshire, som den skotske konge Robert (II) godkendte med en traktat i hans 3.regeringsår (1373/1374). Fik ligeledes 19/7 1378 en traktat på området Findrossie ti
2 CONC l ”John de Forbes, dominus ejusdem” og hans hustru Margaret. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Usikre kilder nævner ham som rektor/forstander og “Laird of Driminor”, sheriff i Aberdeen og skriver ham til området ”That Ilk”. Vistnok død før august 1387. Nogen stamtavler gør far og søn identiske. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT #http://home20.inet.tele.dk/perhag/1000aner/ab293.htm (dead link)
2 CONT #https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clan_Forbes
2 CONT #https://www.hollandhistories.co.uk/forbes (dead link)
2 CONT # http://druminnor.co.uk/pages/history/chronology.php 
2 CONT ## c.1380	Marriage of John de Forbes ‘with the black lip’ and Margaret Chisholm, co-heiress of the Aird.
2 CONT ## 1388	Battle of Otterburn: death of James Earl of Douglas & Mar. John Forbes ‘with the black lip’ knighted.
2 CONT ##1394	Sir John ‘with the black lip’ appointed Crowner (or Colonel) of Aberdeenshire hereditarily.
2 CONT ##1400	Andrew Leslie 4th of Balquhain abducted the Fair Maid of Kemnay, the betrothed of Sir John ‘with the black lip’. The Forbeses destroyed Balquhain Castle; Leslie was tracked down and executed.
2 CONT
